    {
      "@id": "doc:artwork-184336",
      "@type": "schema:CreativeWork",
      "schema:name": {
        "@value": "Labyrinth",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "schema:keywords": {
        "@value": "lands end, labyrinth, people",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "schema:descripption": {
        "@type": "rdf:HTML",
        "@value": "<p>A group of friends walking the Labyrinth at Lands End Park on a sunny day in San Francisco. The image could convey the concept that solving problems can be light and carefree.</p><p>Here is the LIO description of this image:</p><p><b>depicts:</b> people walking a stone labyrinth</p><p><b>shows:</b> rocks arranged in spiral/labyrinth pattern, San Francisco Bay, cargo ship, mountains, clear blue sky, a dog</p><p><b>hasSetting:</b> Land's End, San Francisco, California, USA; daytime, outdoor coastal environment</p><p><b>hasInForeground:</b> stone labyrinth pathway made of rounded rocks arranged in concentric spiral patterns on sandy/gravelly ground</p><p><b>hasInBackground:</b> Golden Gate Bridge, Marin Headlands, San Francisco Bay, red cargo ship on water</p><p><b>hasDepictedBackground:</b> San Francisco Bay with blue water, mountains, and clear sky filling the entire background scene</p><p><b>conveys:</b> mindfulness, contemplation, peaceful exploration, spiritual practice, connection with nature, meditative journey</p><p><b>artisticElement:</b></p><ul><li><b>line:</b> curved, concentric lines formed by stone arrangements creating strong visual rhythm</li><li><b>color:</b> warm earth tones of sand and rock contrasting with vivid blue of sky and water; pink jacket providing a focal color accent</li><li><b>texture:</b> rough, natural textures of rounded stones against sandy ground</li><li><b>composition:</b> leading lines of the labyrinth draw the eye toward the figures and background</li><li><b>scale:</b> human figures provide scale reference against the vast bay and bridge</li></ul><p><b>looksLike:</b> the stone arrangement looksLike a mandala or ancient ceremonial site</p>"
      },
      "schema:creditText": "Margaret Warren",
      "schema:creator": {
        "@id": "doc:person-c"
      },
